          "entry_id": 2973,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.591862,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do I need a referral from a primary care doctor to book with a specialist?\nAnswer: You can book a visit with any of our practitioners without a referral.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2990,
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "similarity_score": 0.36414996,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Medical examinations for work, driving and sport\n\nWe do not carry out commercial driver (DOT) medical examinations, pilot medicals or immigration medical examinations. A sports physical before joining a team or a competition is done in a standard GP appointment.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2977,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3604302,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I do if my insurance isn't listed or I am out-of-network?\nAnswer: You can pay out-of-pocket for your visit, and we can provide you with an itemized receipt to submit to your insurer for potential reimbursement.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2978,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3295887,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "Question: How much will my visit cost if I am paying out-of-pocket?\nAnswer: Out-of-pocket rates are $120 for a General Practitioner (GP) visit, $180 for a Dentist appointment, and $160 for all other specialist consultations.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2991,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.31258565,
          "considered": true,
          "chunk_text": "# Procedure codes and self-pay prices\n## A code you do not recognise\n\nIf your receipt shows a code that is not in this list, the front desk can tell you what it is.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2990,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.31246555,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# General practice services\n## Long-term conditions\n\nIf you live with a long-term condition such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, asthma or COPD, your GP will agree a regular review schedule w",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2974,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3115093,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: What should I bring to my first appointment?\nAnswer: Please bring a valid photo ID, your insurance card, and any relevant prior lab or test results related to your case.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2975,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.3049529,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "Question: Do you offer virtual or telehealth consultations?\nAnswer: No, we currently only offer in-person visits at our clinic location.",
          "text_truncated": false
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2984,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.302027,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Preparing for tests at the clinic\n\nSome tests are done at the clinic during a regular appointment. This guide explains how to prepare for each of them. If your doctor has given you different instruc",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2989,
          "chunk_index": 1,
          "similarity_score": 0.3016373,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Conversations with the chat assistant\n\nConversations with the clinic's chat assistant are kept with your appointment records. Clinic staff can read them, ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2987,
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "similarity_score": 0.29671812,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Appointment reminders and messages from the clinic\n## Messages we will never send\n\nWe will never ask for your card number, bank details, Social Security number or insurance member ID by text message",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2989,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.2962831,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Your privacy and your health information\n## Who can see your medical record\n\nYour record can be seen only by the practitioners and staff involved in your care at the clinic, and by the staff who han",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2982,
          "chunk_index": 5,
          "similarity_score": 0.2916082,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Insurance plan guide\n## Medicare and Medicaid\n\nWe accept Original Medicare (Part B) for medical visits. Medicare does not cover routine dental care, so dental appointments are self-pay for Medicare ",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2988,
          "chunk_index": 0,
          "similarity_score": 0.28726542,
          "considered": false,
          "chunk_text": "# Checking in and registering\n## Registering as a new patient\n\nNew patients fill in three forms at their first visit:\n\n- Form PR-1, New Patient Registration: your contact details, emergency contact an",
          "text_truncated": true
        },
        {
          "entry_id": 2987,
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "similarity_score": 0.2840043,
          "considered": false,
